[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/267494766","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7682#issuecomment-267494766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7682","id":267494766,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NzQ5NDc2Ng==","user":{"login":"francoisfreitag","id":2758243,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NTgyNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2758243?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag","html_url":"https://github.com/francoisfreitag","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-16T01:35:21Z","updated_at":"2016-12-16T01:35:21Z","body":"When test are run in parallel, I cannot spawn another process for the test because `multiprocessing.Pool` spawns daemon processes, which cannot have children.\r\nI'll look for another solution tomorrow. In the meantime, any idea is very welcome.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/267494766/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/267539190","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7682#issuecomment-267539190","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7682","id":267539190,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NzUzOTE5MA==","user":{"login":"aaugustin","id":788910,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODkxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/788910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin","html_url":"https://github.com/aaugustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-16T08:05:05Z","updated_at":"2016-12-16T08:05:05Z","body":"For that kind it used to be acceptable to resort to manual testing, given that it's hard to test initialization code robustly and that such code is rarely modified.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/267539190/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/267805638","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7682#issuecomment-267805638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7682","id":267805638,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NzgwNTYzOA==","user":{"login":"francoisfreitag","id":2758243,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NTgyNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2758243?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag","html_url":"https://github.com/francoisfreitag","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-18T06:15:49Z","updated_at":"2016-12-18T06:15:49Z","body":"The test does not run when the process executing the test is a daemon (when tests are run in parallel). More details can be found in the second commit message.\r\n\r\nI am not sure if it is worth it to include this test. It is easy to run the test using `--parallel=1`, but Jenkins and most people will likely run the tests in parallel. Is there any similar test case that is executed only when tests are run sequentially?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/267805638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/277871081","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7682#issuecomment-277871081","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7682","id":277871081,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3Nzg3MTA4MQ==","user":{"login":"timgraham","id":411869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham","html_url":"https://github.com/timgraham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-02-07T01:20:49Z","updated_at":"2017-02-07T01:20:49Z","body":"I don't think there are any tests that are run conditionally based on the number of parallel tests. Anyway, you can rebase your branch and remove usage of `six`. I'll try to take a closer look later.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/277871081/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/279179315","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7682#issuecomment-279179315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7682","id":279179315,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTE3OTMxNQ==","user":{"login":"francoisfreitag","id":2758243,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NTgyNDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2758243?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag","html_url":"https://github.com/francoisfreitag","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisfreitag/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-02-11T22:07:48Z","updated_at":"2017-02-11T22:07:48Z","body":"I updated the test to use a thread instead of another process, which removes the above limitation (daemonic test runner process unable to spawn an other process to run the test). I can't remember why I discarded this option back then.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/279179315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/282133722","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7682#issuecomment-282133722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7682","id":282133722,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MjEzMzcyMg==","user":{"login":"aaugustin","id":788910,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODkxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/788910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaugustin","html_url":"https://gith